    "verdict": "Scale-free LGH convergence re-examined. The certified lower bound for the order-only (longest-chain) time-separation decays steadily (exponent ~0.37 in N), but the natural-correspondence ceiling decays only ~N^-0.16 (much slower than ell) and is localized to large-proper-time pairs: it is the finite-size fluctuation of the longest-chain estimator, not a support or convention defect. The chain bracket therefore does NOT close and chain-based convergence is not established. The order+count (T7-native) reconstruction decays faster (ceiling ~N^-0.28, bulk 99th percentile ~N^-0.41, consistent with Poisson counting) and falls below the chain ceiling from N=16. The obstruction is therefore estimator-specific: the convergence question depends on which discrete time-separation reconstruction is used, not on the directed-distance convention (already corrected by QR-05CZ). No metric, continuum, curvature or gravity claim."
